<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f77daadec4f408f1389e7dc5ec4afdb2dba33f256dc96cc4a3402125656dc852</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, France agree on deal to support Europe's struggling car industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284fa29cf92820bcfc86bba73de016ae35f7113c8d3851541b91ef57c0599efb</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595--5e23597ac466.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two countries said the agreement aimed to safeguard Europe's automotive industry, encouraging development and research. Automakers in Europe have so far struggled to compete with Chinese electric car companies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German lawmakers back monthly state pension contributions for children, with families able to add more.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada53c0b3571a2360a16c8c0ee9d4bda146fbc268833b6ab85c848bf8ce228b2</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-mor/live-79678671--02713419dab3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-more/live-79678671?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's parliament has backed a plan to help children save for retirement from the age of 6. Meanwhile, Jewish students report death threats after they confronted a far-right lawmaker.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hamburg court jails 2 men over plot to attack Jewish leaders on behalf of Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e030194197839787ef15c8c086278f993befeec88e69693a6cd721de0b7d31d0</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895--ad75d24ae5e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The men were found guilty of espionage and attempted murder. According to the court, they planned to attack the president of the Central Council of Jews in Germany and president of the German-Israeli society.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Train station alcohol ban comes into force</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c1e1d06f52001e0f4083a620db33980470799753df9ca021418e151df8c640e</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807--e7db446fe401.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Consuming alcohol is no longer permitted at train stations in Germany, to improve the lot of travelers and staff alike. Coalition talks are restarting in Berlin, and an inmate is loose in Essen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Isha Bhatia Sanan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c66e8e49bdaf78c47483e208fe4a349f2193078200e7b92b9e22fd06c1652b5</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/isha-bhatia-sanan/a-79678415--251eb4c8b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/isha-bhatia-sanan/a-79678415?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Isha Bhatia Sanan is DW’s Bureau Chief in India, leading the broadcaster’s operations in Delhi and Chennai.</summary><category term="Our Experts" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6f888e66d991584636e855832edceea23e28b31d53d6d5413575c04f8ccd9ee</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of German gamblers could sue for their money back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47bf3753f99056973b4f8cee670b5879ed3e3eb8f244beaa28cac641c92d7d90</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844--bc7691d0e6e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German gamblers may finally be able to beat the house, thanks to new court rulings in the EU and in Germany. The decisions could help gambling addicts — but the legal road might be difficult.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
